2.3.m:
Sūta said:
In the Kali age, a man of little wealth [may perform] a consecration to be accomplished in one day;
the excellent Tantric practitioner should perform an immediate preliminary consecration with clarified butter.

He should perform the installation of the breath of life, and make the oblation according to rule;
he should present the priestly fee according to rule, and immediately after, the final full offering.
Description of the consecration of deities and others

his wealth will be lost, or his prosperity ruined;
in severe torment from illness, oppression by the king, and imprisonment,
the destruction of his elephants, horses, cattle, and servants will surely occur.

Teeth that stand above other teeth, encroaching upon the row,
all of those cause harm, as do those shaped like darts;
and all those that are supplementary teeth do not cause harm anywhere.
